+# Master-goal slice — daily paid-work quota (Codex ≤30%) + CPU load in PC-health guard — 2026-09-22
+
+## Task
+Implementation/test slice for the master goal: enforce "Codex is fallback only and must stay at or below 30% of daily AI-agent work; prefer Claude/OpenCode", "never use paid APIs or paid GPU", and "PC HEALTH AND ZERO-CHAOS GUARD must measure CPU load, available RAM and free disk before and after every delegated local session". Fix only safe root causes, add focused regression tests, report evidence, no production deployment.
+
+## Why
+Current master already: never drives ChatGPT/claude-desktop programmatically, requires explicit `allowPaid` for Codex, prefers free cloud/local agents in the default plan, and wraps every dispatch in the shared zero-chaos session guard. Two explicit master-goal requirements are NOT enforced and are now added: (1) a persistent daily paid-work quota with a 30% paid cap so Codex can never dominate daily AI-agent work, and (2) real CPU-load measurement (with warning/critical thresholds) so heavy local work is deferred under CPU pressure exactly like RAM pressure already is.
+
+## Current state
+Branch `ai/master-coordinator/opencode-1790037903647-a1`, tree clean at `d06cb3ed` (coordinator default HEAD/LKG). `scripts/master-coordinator.cjs` dispatches OpenCode/OpenHuman/AnythingLLM/free-cloud/Codex but has no daily quota ledger; `lib/agent-session-guard.js` measures free RAM + free disk on every preflight/postflight but reports no CPU load. Before-session PC health captured: free RAM 26.7%, free disk ~187 GB, Desktop clean.
+
+## Target state
+- A small append-only JSONL work-quota ledger (`lib/agent-work-quota.js`, `state/agent-work-quota.jsonl`) counts every dispatched agent work unit (free vs paid) over a trailing window (default 24h) and blocks a new Codex dispatch when one more paid unit would push the paid share above the cap (default 30%). Free agents (OpenCode, OpenHuman, AnythingLLM, world-cloud-ai, Claude/desktop via reportSelfExecuted) are never throttled.
+- The PC-health guard measures CPU load via a cross-platform `os.cpus()` tick sample (`lib/resource-scheduler.js#cpuUtilizationPercent`) and surfaces `cpuPercent`/`cpuWarning`/`cpuCritical` in every preflight/postflight, deferring `localHeavy` work when CPU is critically saturated, mirroring the existing RAM deferral.
+- All new logic pure/unit-tested; no behavior change for free agents; no production deployment.
+
+## Files / systems involved
+- `lib/agent-work-quota.js` (new) — pure daily paid-work-quota ledger.
+- `lib/resource-scheduler.js` — added `sampleCpuTicks`/`cpuBusyRatio`/`cpuUtilizationPercent`.
+- `lib/agent-session-guard.js` — `snapshotResources` now includes CPU load + thresholds; preflight `throttle` also gates `localHeavy` on `cpuCritical`.
+- `data/desktop-ai-policy.json` — added `warnCpuPercent`/`maxCpuPercent`/`cpuSampleIntervalMs` under `sessionHygiene`.
+- `scripts/master-coordinator.cjs` — quota gate + recording for Codex/free agents and self-executed Claude work; `PAID_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` is a pending (never false-green) result.
+- `test/agent-work-quota.test.js` (new), `test/master-coordinator.test.js`, `test/resource-scheduler.test.js`, `test/agent-session-guard.test.js` — focused regression tests.
+
+## Known risks
+- Quota ledger lives in git-ignored `state/` (like `ai-agent-reports.jsonl`), so quota history is per-machine runtime state, not source truth.
+- A Codex attempt counts as a paid unit as soon as the quota gate + allow-paid gate pass, even if the CLI is missing or the run later fails — deliberately conservative so the paid budget is never exceeded.
+- CPU sampling adds a bounded ~150ms sample per preflight/postflight; only the session guard path uses it.
+- Process detection/killing for orphan duplicate agents remains config/policy-only (never broaden deletion or kill unknown/user processes).
+
+## Golden systems that must be preserved
+Existing routing, leases, resource scheduling, session guard, reports schema, `OFFLINE_ONLY_AGENTS` never-invoked contract, default free-only plan (OpenCode + OpenHuman; cloud/AnythingLLM/Codex opt-in), Codex explicit `allowPaid` gate, deny-by-default paid dispatch, `npm run check` gates.
+
+## Errors that must not return
+Paid Codex work exceeding 30% of the trailing daily window; Codex auto-selection as primary; false-green PASS for a quota-blocked subtask; `state/` runtime files committed to the repo; Desktop clutter/worktrees; CPU sampling failing closed on platforms where `os.cpus()` ticks do not advance.
+
+## Exact patch / change plan
+1. Add `lib/agent-work-quota.js`: `record`/`readRecords`/`snapshot`/`decidePaidDispatch`, paid-only = `codex` by class, 30%/24h defaults, tolerant of malformed lines and missing files.
+2. Add `cpuUtilizationPercent` (+ tick helpers) to `lib/resource-scheduler.js`.
+3. Surface CPU load + thresholds in `lib/agent-session-guard.js` and add policy keys to `data/desktop-ai-policy.json`.
+4. Wire quota into `scripts/master-coordinator.cjs`: record free units on dispatch, record/window-check paid units in `invokeCodex`, `PAID_QUOTA_EXCEEDED` as a pending result, env knobs `MASTER_COORDINATOR_CODEX_MAX_SHARE`/`MASTER_COORDINATOR_QUOTA_WINDOW_HOURS`/`AI_AGENT_WORK_QUOTA_PATH`.
+5. Add regression tests for quota math/boundaries, coordinator integration without CLI spawn, CPU math/measurement, and guard snapshot.
+6. Update this WIP entry, run focused + repository checks, commit, push, open PR. No merge or production deploy.
+
+## Tests to run
+- `node --test test/agent-work-quota.test.js test/master-coordinator.test.js test/resource-scheduler.test.js test/agent-session-guard.test.js`
+- `npm run check:fast`
+- `npm run check`
+- `npm run desktop-ai:check`
+- `npm run check-agent-rules`
+- `git diff --check`
+
+## Deployment / PR plan
+Branch `ai/master-coordinator/opencode-1790037903647-a1` -> PR to `master`. No direct master push, no auto-merge, no production deployment. Runtime ledger stays in git-ignored `state/`.
+
+## Current progress
+All code and tests written. Focused verification next; no claim of robustness against a live free-agent benchmark (out of scope for this slice and honestly not exercised).
+
+## Next action
+Run focused tests and repository gates, inspect failures, fix until PASS, then `git diff --check`, commit, push, open the review PR. Leave quota CLI/cloud integration as a separately reviewed follow-up.
+
+## Completion criteria
+- Paid >=30% cap enforced with an append-only ledger; free agents never throttled.
+- Preflight/postflight report real CPU load; `localHeavy` work defers under critical CPU.
+- No accepted quality metric regresses; focused + repository checks pass; PR open with evidence.
+- No production deployment performed and no `state/` runtime files committed.
+
+## Final evidence
+Pending current-run verification: focused test output, `npm run check` result, `golden:check`, `desktop-ai:check`, `check-agent-rules`, `git diff --check`, after-session PC health, PR URL, and the honest list of not-claimed items.
+
